TITLE:: FxHintBar
summary:: a strip that says what the mouse is over
categories:: Libraries>ParaEQ
related:: Classes/ParaEQGUI, Classes/CompressorGUI, Classes/FxChainGUI, Classes/ModuleHintBar

DESCRIPTION::
A line along the bottom of a window that describes whatever control the pointer
is on, so a window full of small boxes can be read without a manual. The same
idea as link::Classes/ModuleHintBar:: in the module family, written here so this
repository depends on nothing.

code::
hints = FxHintBar();
hints.watch(window);                    // once, after the window exists
window.layout = VLayout(..., hints.view);

hints.attach(box, "what this box does");
hints.attach([label, slider, box], "the three parts of one control");
hints.attach(readout, { "now at " ++ thing.value });   // worked out on hover
::

link::#-attach:: answers what it was given, so a control can be wrapped where it
is built. A hint is a String, or a Function answering one.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: defaultString
What the bar says when the pointer is on nothing in particular.
ARGUMENT:: height
In pixels; link::#*defaultHeight:: if left out.

METHOD:: defaultHeight
22.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: view
The strip, to put in a layout.

METHOD:: watch
Let a window pass its children's mouse-overs down, and reset the bar when the
pointer is over the window itself.

METHOD:: attach
Give one or more views a hint. Answers code::views::.

METHOD:: string
What the bar says now; nil puts back the default.

METHOD:: clear
METHOD:: defaultString
METHOD:: visible

METHOD:: toggle
A checkbox that folds the bar away, made on the first ask. It has to sit outside
the bar, or folding it would take the way back with it.
